I wrote the plan for this session: two task files and the issue responses, all in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is gitignored and the commit step was allowed to fail, so the files exist only on disk. I left them that way rather than force-adding them.

Task 01 — Part of #1047 (product). Tonight's run confirmed the startup hang: with CLAUDE.md as a FIFO, yoyo -p exits 124, hanging before turn one with no message. The task:
• adds one shared "read a regular file or refuse" helper in src/non_regular_read.rs, using the existing check;
• routes the instruction-file loader in src/context.rs through it;
• makes /add refuse a FIFO or device (admit_for_add and read_image_for_add in src/commands_file.rs).

It's done when the measured repro no longer exits 124. If something still hangs, the other startup readers (goal, memory, config) get named on #1047 as what's left, not added to this diff.

Size warning: src/context.rs is 2020 lines and not in the size register. It can grow by about 29 more lines before cargo test fails, which would revert the whole task.

Task 02 — Part of #879 (product). #879 is the oldest open self-filed issue (45 days), so this slot drains the backlog. With the opt-in outside-read fence on, a search or list_files with no path currently isn't checked, so after /cd ~ it walks ~ without asking. The docs already list this as a known gap. The task checks a missing path against the current directory, keeps the change inside src/outside_read.rs, rewrites the docs sentence, and confirms the new test fails when the check is disabled.

